Session 35 summary — three zero_silent_loss root causes diagnosed with instrumented proof; two fixed and verified, the third fix is built awaiting test.

**Fix 1 (verified):** `mxfs_dir_buf_is_undestaged` judged "safe to refresh" by comparing the local `li_lsn` against the LSN stamped in the dir block payload — but peers stamp that field from their own journals, so the compare is meaningless cross-node. The P35A probe proved every false verdict had `li_lsn < payload_lsn` (impossible within one journal), and each one let `xfs_da_read_buf` re-read disk over the node's own committed-unwritten dirent inserts — losing a dirent within 7ms of its own mkdir. Replaced the LSN heuristic with a node-local logged/written sequence pair on the buffer (bumped in `xfs_trans_log_buf`, snapshotted at write submit). Result: in-AIL refreshes and create errors dropped to zero.

**Fix 2 (verified):** release drains stalled the whole cluster 23-29s because `xfs_bwrite` on a pinned buffer sleeps in `wait_unpin` without driving the CIL — the unpin only came at the ~30s log-worker tick. Added an async `xfs_log_force` before the bwrite in both dir-block flush loops. Max drain fell from 29s to 135ms; iter walls dropped from 166s to 102-123s, better than the previous record.

**Root 3 (proven, fix untested):** the residual ~1 durable loss per iter. The P35E write-lineage probe ruled out out-of-hold writes and SCST cache lag; the mechanism is fast-path EX creates re-dirtying dir blocks during the BAST drain, after the durability fence but before the single-shot stale pass — the release then hands off the lock with committed-unwritten dirents (189 `P99-STALE-SKIP` fires per iter), and the divergent images clobber each other. Fix in build `FCDB6848`: the stale pass now reports skips and the release loops flush→stale until a clean pass.

Next session: deploy `FCDB6848`, run the 3-iter criterion, and if clean, strip the P35x probes (P35E is un-ratelimited) and proceed to the full ship gate. Criteria not met yet — the marker stays unwritten and the relay continues.

